   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the real property tax law and the administrative code of the city of New York, in relation to extending a real property tax abatement program for certain commercial properties in cities having a population of one million or more and in relation to extending a special reduction under the commercial rent tax in the city of New York",
    "basePrintNo": "S7135",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7135-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§499-a, 499-c & 499-d, RPT L; amd §11-704, NYC Ad Cd",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Tax Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S7135\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the real property tax law and the administrative code\nof the city of New York, in relation to extending a real property tax\nabatement program for certain commercial properties in cities having a\npopulation of one million or more and in relation to extending a\nspecial reduction under the commercial rent tax in the city of New\nYork\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nThis bill would extend for four years a real property tax abatement\nprogram and a commercial rental tax reduction for certain commercial\nproperties in designated areas of the City of New York.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nThis bill would to amend the Real Property Tax Law and the New York\nCity Administrative Code, to extend a real property tax abatement\nprogram and a commercial rental tax reduction for certain commercial\nproperties in cities having a population of one million\n\nSection 1 of the bill would extend the real property tax abatement\nbenefit period from March 31, 2016 to March 31, 2020 and the\neligibility period from March 31, 2010 to March 31, 2014.\n\nSection 2 of the bill would extend the time period in which\nexpenditures or improvements. to eligible premises and common areas of\neligible buildings must be made to qualify for the real property tax\nabatement from September 30, 2010 to September 30, 2014.\n\nSection 3 of the bill subjects leases commencing after April 1, 1997\nto any amendments made to the provisions of article 4, title 4 of the\nreal property tax law should the bill become law.\n\nSection 4 extends the benefit period for a special reduction in the\ncommercial rent tax in the New York City Administrative Code from\nMarch 31, 2015 to March 31, 2020.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThe purpose of this program is to assist in New York City's economic\nrecovery and job creation by encouraging relocation and expansion of\nbusinesses to Lower Manhattan.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew in 2010.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone to the State.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately, provided it shall become law after April 1, 2010, it\nshall be deemed to have been in full force and effect on and after\nApril 1, 2010.\n",
